From: Chris Hibbert <hibbert@kwi.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jun 1994 09:27:15 -0700
Subject: [#94-6-57] An Advertising Counter-Flame 

I've thought all along that the mistake that the lawyers made was not advertising
on the net.  If you are sufficiently circumspect, and post in the right places,
and try to act like you're adding to the discussion, rather than being blatantly
inconsiderate, then you can advertise and not get more than a few complaints.  The
thing you're not allowed to do is to cross-post widely, or to post anything in
wildly inappropriate places.  The ad about the Green Card lottery was obviously
re-posted to every possible group, and no attempt was made to find even remotely
relevant groups.  That's what made people mad.

Why has everyone else missed this in the popular press, and the discussions I've
seen on the net?

Chris

